  "name": "enum-group-deletion-moves-one-step",
  "description": "A constant is reported only where deleting it, alone or with the others reported, leaves a program that builds and denotes the same value at every name it uses. A later constant of the block must then drop by exactly one, which holds for iota plus or minus untyped constants and for the plain name of such a constant, and must stay a valid constant of its type. A member whose deletion would move a later constant any other way, push it below its type's least value, make an expression after it divide by zero or shift by a negative count, or break a repeated list of several names, is retained. An unnamed constant that is the only name of a specification stating the list the next specification repeats is reported, at any place in its block, a member or a constant a function body declares, because replacing its name with a blank one moves nothing: its finding is manual while a constant repeating its list is named, and deletable with the members that repeat it where none is. A member whose deletion moves no constant code names, or moves one only by one step under an alias, is reported, and so is a constant no enumerated type holds whose deletion moves no named constant.",
